.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark scratch: per-read and per-probe intermediates. The summary each run produces
# is the record; these are regenerated on every run and were previously being staged --
# v60_shape/spool alone contributed 2856 files to one commit.
#
# The binaries are here too for the same reason. v61_burst keeps a pair of 300 KB builds so
# it can alternate between two commits without rebuilding; they are reproducible from the
# refs named in the script.
reports/gateab_ab/**/spool/
reports/gateab_ab/**/k3_noburst
reports/gateab_ab/**/k3_burst
reports/gateab_ab/**/steady58

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures are PART OF THE REPOSITORY and must survive every rule above.
#
# `make test` is this project's correctness gate, and it deliberately runs without model
# weights, but only if the fixtures are present in the clone. Without these re-includes
# the rules above silently drop tests/fixtures/{cache,st}/ (synthetic .safetensors
# shards), expert_trace.bin, and the recorded reference logs. A fresh clone would then
# build cleanly and fail its own test suite, which is a bad first impression and a
# confusing one to debug.
!tests/fixtures/
!tests/fixtures/**

# medium-ladder build artifacts
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/probe
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/probe.c
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/expert_pread
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/expert_pread.c
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/seq_pread
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/seq_pread.c
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/run.log
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/run*.log
benchmarks/medium-ladder-out/expert_offsets.py

# 探针编译产物与 Windows 重解析点（git 无法读取 ReparsePoint 内容）
reports/**/nvmebench
reports/**/bench.latest.log
reports/**/*.exe
